# --- Test fixtures extracted from production ---------------------------------
BackEnd/incident-service/src/test/resources/fixtures/**/*.csv
# custom_values.csv is HAND-AUTHORED and synthetic (the real export was unusable —
# extracted on the wrong column). It is unregenerable, so it IS tracked.
!BackEnd/incident-service/src/test/resources/fixtures/custom_values.csv
# ref_custom_field_enum.csv / ref_user.csv are synthetic on the same argument, and a
# stronger one: redmine.custom_field_enumerations, users and email_addresses were never
# delivered at all, so there is no export to regenerate them from. The names and addresses
# in them are machine-generated placeholders, not staff. Tracked.
# (Production seeds come from scripts/extract-ref-tables.py and stay ignored above.)
!BackEnd/incident-service/src/test/resources/fixtures/ref_custom_field_enum.csv
!BackEnd/incident-service/src/test/resources/fixtures/ref_user.csv

